        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(lmstudio): map trained_for_tool_use into compat.supportsTools",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLM Studio discovery already reads `capabilities.trained_for_tool_use`, but only uses it for the display `tool-use` name tag. Catalog `compat` did not set `supportsTools`, so core's permissive default (`supportsTools !== false`) still offered tools for models that report `trained_for_tool_use: false`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMirror the Venice catalog contract: when the upstream capability is an explicit boolean, write `compat.supportsTools` accordingly. Omitted metadata stays unset so older/unknown entries keep the permissive default.\n\n## User Impact\n\nModels that LM Studio marks as not trained for tool use no longer advertise tools. Models that report `true` set `supportsTools: true` explicitly. Unspecified capability is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Proof | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | `mapLmstudioWireEntry`: true → `supportsTools: true`; false → `false`; omitted → unset | pass |\n| L2 | `discoverLmstudioModels` path spreads `base.compat` (incl. tools) + `supportsUsageInStreaming` | pass |\n| Gate | `oxfmt` + `oxlint` + focused vitest on `models.test.ts` | pass |\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/lmstudio/src/models.ts extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts\npnpm exec oxlint extensions/lmstudio/src/models.ts extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts -t \"maps trained_for_tool_use|discovers llm models and maps metadata\"\n→ 2 passed\n```\n\nHead: `d2ca8162e7b0ee7837d731512e670927c7af1e92`  \nCompare: 2 files only (`models.ts` + `models.test.ts`).\n",
